# Build outputs.
_novo/

# The generated API page.  `novo doc` writes it here so you can read
# what the registry will serve; the registry gets its own copy, uploaded
# beside the archive by `novo pkg publish`.  It is generated from the
# sources, so committing it would be committing a second original.
APIDOC.md

# The built package binary — `novo pkg build` names it after the
# package.  This package is a LIBRARY and builds none; the line is here
# for when it grows a `main` and it does.
/arrow-nv

# NOT novo.lock.  A locked build resolves the same closure twice and
# does it offline once the cache is warm, and a consumer never reads a
# dependency's lock — they resolve their own closure and write their
# own — so committing it costs nobody anything and makes this
# repository's CI reproducible.  It is not on the publish allow-list, so
# it never ships either way.
